  "explanation": {
    "md_es": [
      "**Preguntar:** *What time is it?* (¿qué hora es?) · *What time is the class?* (¿a qué hora es la clase?)",
      "",
      "**Responder:** *It's + hora.*",
      "",
      "| Hora | Se dice |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| 8:00 | It's eight o'clock. |",
      "| 8:10 | It's ten past eight. |",
      "| 8:15 | It's quarter past eight. |",
      "| 8:20 | It's twenty past eight. |",
      "| 8:30 | It's half past eight. |",
      "| 8:40 | It's twenty to nine. |",
      "| 8:45 | It's quarter to nine. |",
      "",
      "- Hasta y media se usa **past**; después de y media, **to** (la hora siguiente).",
      "- También se puede decir como en un reloj digital: *eight forty*.",
      "- Para eventos: **at** + hora → *at nine o'clock*."
    ],
    "common_mistakes_es": [
      {
        "wrong": "It's the eight.",
        "right": "It's eight o'clock.",
        "note": "En español 'son las ocho'; en inglés no hay artículo."
      },
      {
        "wrong": "It are eight o'clock.",
        "right": "It's eight o'clock.",
        "note": "Siempre 'it is', aunque sean varias horas."
      }
    ],
    "false_friends": []
  },
